            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="0730" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.857/150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-26T16:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Department’s telegrams 33 of March 21 and 35 of March 23. The Government of
                    Panama is in full agreement with procedure and drafts proposed by the
                    Department. The Dominican Government has notified Panama of its full approval.
                    Garay will proceed to circulate the documents by air mail as soon as possible
                    requesting telegraphic replies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
